Third-party code
----------------

third_party/featurevis/

    featurevis, from https://github.com/cajal/featurevis
    Copyright (c) 2019 Cajal MICrONS Team
    MIT License — the original text is retained unmodified at
    third_party/featurevis/LICENSE and governs that directory.

    MODIFIED. One change from upstream:

        featurevis/ops.py    scipy.signal.gaussian
                          -> scipy.signal.windows.gaussian
                             (4 call sites: lines 207, 208, 424, 426)

    The upstream spelling was removed in SciPy 1.13. The replacement exists on
    both sides of that removal, so the patched copy runs under either and no
    version pin is needed.

    Nothing else in that directory differs from upstream.


Code that is NOT derived from the repositories deposited with Fu et al. (2026)
------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Three of those repositories carry no license — jiakunf/Fu_et_al_2026,
lucabaroni/center-surround and sinzlab/probabilistic-center-surround — and
nothing here is copied from any of them. The mask construction in
csartifact/mask.py is an independent implementation of an algorithm their paper
describes, and csartifact/optimize.py's ChangeSurroundStd is an independent
reimplementation of an operation absent from public featurevis. The full
provenance audit, with its check date and evidence, is in DEVIATIONS.md under
D3.
